# OWASP Top 10:2025 (hard rule)

Before implementing a feature, check it against every item below. If a
change would weaken one, stop and say so instead of shipping it.

| Risk | Do this |
|---|---|
| A01 Access control | Admin routes: `auth({ guards: ['web'] })` + `middleware.can({ permission })`; record rules in a policy. Customer `:id` routes: `customerOwns` + queries scoped by session customer (404, not 403). Never trust owner ids from the client. Permission grants must not exceed the actor; see below. |
| A02 Misconfiguration | No new secrets in code; add env vars to `start/env.ts` and `.env.example`. Keep CSP/CSRF/HSTS on; no inline styles/scripts. No stack traces outside dev/test. |
| A03 Supply chain | `yarn add` only well-maintained packages; commit `yarn.lock`. Run `yarn security:audit` after dependency changes. Pin GitHub Action SHAs. |
| A04 Crypto | Secrets at rest via `encryption.encrypt(value, { purpose })`; one-time codes hashed (HMAC/hash), compared with `timingSafeEqual`. Never log or return secrets (`serializeAs: null`, `auditHidden`). |
| A05 Injection | Vine validator on every input (see `validator-strict-types.mdc`). Raw SQL only with bindings; whitelist sort keys; `containsPattern()` for LIKE. Rich text: `sanitizeEditorHtml` on save, `sanitizeHtml` (DOMPurify) before `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. |
| A06 Insecure design | Rate-limit new public/expensive/auth endpoints in `start/limiter.ts`. Guard every public form with invisible reCAPTCHA (`public-form-recaptcha.mdc`). Money/stock changes in one repository transaction; recompute totals server-side; idempotency for retries. Build external URLs from `APP_URL`, never `Host`. |
| A07 Authentication | Sensitive changes (email, password, MFA) need the current password; password changes bump `sessionVersion`. New passwords use `newPasswordSchema()`; login passwords `currentPasswordSchema()`. Regenerate session on login/logout. |
| A08 Integrity | Uploads: validate extension/size in Vine, store via `uploadImage()` (re-encodes, server Content-Type). Verify webhook signatures and amounts before acting. |
| A09 Logging | Record security events with `AuditLogService.recordSecurityEvent`; alert-worthy ones log `warn` with an `event` field. Add new sensitive keys to `SENSITIVE_KEYS` in `config/logger.ts`. |
| A10 Exceptions | Never swallow errors (`.catch(() => null)`, empty `catch {}`). Use `orNullIfMissing()` for not-found; log best-effort failures; await or `void` every promise. Fail closed. |

## A01: granting permissions

A management permission such as `roles.edit` is not a grant of every permission in the catalogue. Staff may create a custom role (`roles.create`): `RoleService.create` saves a name only, and the role starts with no permissions. The escalation is filling that role in.

In `RolePolicy.editPermissions` and `UserPolicy.update`, for anyone who is not the locked admin (`user.isAdmin`):

- Refuse edits to the actor's own role.
- Refuse `granted` when `!user.hasPermission(permission)`.
- Refuse granting or assigning `users.*`, `roles.*`, or `themes.*` (`isAdminOnlyPermission` in `app/abilities/permissions.ts`).

Apply both checks on the role matrix and on staff role assignment. The matrix and the user role picker only hide choices the policy rejects. Revoking a permission on someone else's role may stay allowed.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — roles.edit alone, so the actor can grant customers.view to their own role
if (!user.hasPermission('roles.edit')) return false
if (role.isLocked) return AuthorizationResponse.deny('The admin role always has every permission', 422)
return true

// ✅ GOOD — own role, admin-only namespaces, then permissions the actor lacks
if (role.id === user.roleId && !user.isAdmin) {
  return AuthorizationResponse.deny("You can't change your own role", 422)
}
if (change.granted && isAdminOnlyPermission(change.permission) && !user.isAdmin) {
  return AuthorizationResponse.deny('Only admins can grant this permission', 422)
}
if (change.granted && !user.hasPermission(change.permission)) {
  return AuthorizationResponse.deny("You can't grant a permission you don't have", 422)
}
```

## Before finishing

- State which OWASP items the feature touches and how each is handled.
- New endpoints: validator, guard/ownership, limiter (if public or auth), transformer (no raw models).
